hwmon: cix: add safe ACPI fan control

Expose the CIXHA024 firmware fan interface through standard hwmon PWM
semantics.  Radxa Orion firmware uses a no-argument private EC getter with
a 0..128 result and 0xff failure sentinel, while generic CIX firmware uses
a two-argument getter with a 0..100 result and 0xffffffff sentinel.  Select
the format from the private method signature, but invoke only the public
CIXHA024 wrapper.

Map pwm_enable according to the documented hwmon ABI: 0 is uncontrolled
full speed, 1 is manual PWM control, and 2 is automatic control.  Do not
expose the firmware mute method as mode 0.  Keep the mode unknown until a
successful write because the firmware has no reliable mode query.  Validate
all method results, ranges, sentinels and optional generic-firmware status
returns.

